- S2-DEV-01: Customer List with Search and Filter
- S2-DEV-02: Customer Create and Edit Form

### UI/UX Tasks

- S2-UIX-01: Customer Wireframes

### Testing Tasks

- S2-TST-01: Customer Module Test Cases

### Scrum Master Tasks

- S2-SM-01: Sprint 2 Planning Notes and Update Sprint Board

## Sprint Board Organization

Organize Sprint 2 issues according to their current progress:

- Todo: Tasks that have not yet started.
- In Progress: Tasks currently being worked on.
- In Review: Tasks awaiting review, testing, or approval.
- Done: Tasks that have met their acceptance criteria and Definition of Done.

## Team Responsibilities

- Scrum Master: Organize sprint activities, monitor progress, update the project board, and coordinate with team members.
- Developers: Implement assigned features and submit pull requests for review.
- UI/UX Designer: Prepare wireframes and design specifications.
- Tester: Review developer implementations, execute test cases, and report bugs and testing results.

## Sprint Planning Activities

- Identify and organize Sprint 2 tasks.
- Create individual GitHub Issues for assigned activities.
- Define task descriptions and acceptance criteria.
- Assign responsibilities to the appropriate team members.
- Apply appropriate labels and priorities.
- Organize issues in the GitHub Project board.
- Monitor task progress and identify potential blockers.

## Definition of Done

- Assigned requirements are completed.
- Acceptance criteria are satisfied.
- Required testing and verification are performed.
- Identified issues are addressed or documented.
- Required reviews and approvals are obtained.
- GitHub Issues and Project board statuses are updated.

## Completion

Sprint 2 planning and board organization have been completed. Tasks have been documented and organized in GitHub Issues and the Project board to support progress tracking, team coordination, and sprint monitoring.
